From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheKit <thekit@disroot.org>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:23:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: probe wifi0 in emulated HAL interface list

Waydroid's emulated wlan netdev is named "wifi0" rather than "wlan0": the
host kernel's vendor wifi driver (e.g. MTK gen4m) matches interfaces by the
"wlan"/"p2p" name prefixes in its namespace-global netdev/inetaddr notifiers
and dereferences the container veth's netdev_priv() as its own struct,
panicking the host on the first RTM_NEWADDR.

Add "wifi0" to the names the emulator wifi HAL probes under /sys/class/net,
alongside the existing wlan0/wlan1, so it discovers the interface.

Change-Id: I9e48540bd58b5a570047f019a5be653ee33e6f1b
---
 wifi/wifi_hal/info.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wifi/wifi_hal/info.cpp b/wifi/wifi_hal/info.cpp
index 8869c65..fb89be0 100644
--- a/wifi/wifi_hal/info.cpp
+++ b/wifi/wifi_hal/info.cpp
@@ -20,7 +20,10 @@
 
 #include <string>
 
-static const char* const kInterfaceNames[] = {"wlan0", "wlan1"};
+// "wifi0" can be used to avoid the wlan"/"p2p" prefixes
+// that host-kernel vendor wifi drivers match in their namespace-global
+// netdev notifiers (which panics on the container's veth).
+static const char* const kInterfaceNames[] = {"wlan0", "wlan1", "wifi0"};
 
 Info::Info() {
     mInterfaces.reserve(sizeof(kInterfaceNames) / sizeof(kInterfaceNames[0]));
